<h3 class=3D"post-title entry-title">
ECG Interpretation Review - #1 (LVH, Strain, Ischemia, LAE, RAE, RVH, LAA, =
RAA)
</h3>
<div class=3D"post-header">
<div class=3D"post-header-line-1"></div>
</div>
<div class=3D"post-body entry-content" id=3D"post-body-5465054651676140672"=
>
<b>&nbsp;</b>-------------------------------<br>
<b>QUESTION:</b> Interpret the 12-lead ECG below.<br>
<ul>
<li>Clinically - What do you <i>suspect</i> this patient has?</li>
</ul>
<table cellpadding=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" class=3D"tr-caption-container" s=
tyle=3D"float: left; margin-right: 1em; text-align: left;"><tbody>
<tr><td style=3D"text-align: center;"><a href=3D"https://blogger.googleuser=
content.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhZbMi-Xtst4yOODVdYhiczgujhNWPGcm2Oqd8PjZ7q=
muKcuI6Zq2KoKMMwrAempx1BCKXZFQbkIpsWsdg-K-NIrDZT7XV-jbAEQhNWJ93inNNRdnvybjl=
76j0S5ZqwABiXjRc4-lgSUPc/s1600/ECG+Interpretation+Review+-+1+-+LVH%252C+str=
ain%252C+ischemia%252C+LAE%252C+RAE%252C+LAA.jpg" imageanchor=3D"1" style=
=3D"clear: left; margin-bottom: 1em; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;=
"><img border=3D"0" height=3D"224" src=3D"https://blogger.googleusercontent=
.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhZbMi-Xtst4yOODVdYhiczgujhNWPGcm2Oqd8PjZ7qmuKcuI6=
Zq2KoKMMwrAempx1BCKXZFQbkIpsWsdg-K-NIrDZT7XV-jbAEQhNWJ93inNNRdnvybjl76j0S5Z=
qwABiXjRc4-lgSUPc/s400/ECG+Interpretation+Review+-+1+-+LVH%252C+strain%252C=
+ischemia%252C+LAE%252C+RAE%252C+LAA.jpg" width=3D"400"></a></td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"tr-caption" style=3D"text-align: center;"><span style=3D"f=
ont-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"><b>(</b>ECG re=
produced from <a href=3D"http://www.ecg2014.com/" target=3D"_blank">ECG-201=
4-ePub</a>&nbsp;- pg 40A<b>)</b></span><br>
<span style=3D"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;=
"><b>- <span class=3D"Apple-style-span" style=3D"color: #e06666;">Note</spa=
n> - </b><i>Enlarge by clicking on Figures -</i></span></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<div style=3D"text-align: justify;">
<b>INTERPRETATION:</b>&nbsp; The rhythm is sinus at ~75/minute.&nbsp; The P=
R, QRS, and QT intervals are normal.&nbsp; There is <b>RAD (</b><i>predomin=
antly negative QRS in lead I; positive in aVF</i><b>)</b>.</div>
<ul>
<li style=3D"text-align: justify;"><b><span class=3D"Apple-style-span" styl=
e=3D"color: #e06666;">Chamber Enlargement</span> - </b>The P wave is tall, =
peaked, and looks <i>"uncomfortable to sit on"</i> in lead II =3D <b>RAA</b=
>.&nbsp; There is a <i>deep</i> negative component to the P wave in lead V1=
 =3D <b>LAA</b>. There is obvious <b><i>voltage</i></b> for <b>LVH (</b><i>=
the S in V2 plus the R in V5&gt;&gt;35</i><b>)</b>.&nbsp; We <i>also</i> su=
spect <b>RVH (</b><i>because of the presence of otherwise unexplained RAD i=
n this patient who has multiple chamber enlargement</i><b>)</b>.</li>
<li style=3D"text-align: justify;"><b>Q-R-S-T Changes - </b>are clearly con=
sistent with <b>LV <i>"<span class=3D"Apple-style-span" style=3D"color: #e0=
6666;">strain</span>"</i></b>, especially in leads V5, V6 <b>(</b><i>asymme=
tric ST-T depression</i><b>)</b>.&nbsp; The fact that T wave inversion is s=
o diffuse, tends toward being <i>symmetric</i> in leads I, aVL, V3 and V4 w=
ith ST coving and J-point depression in V5,V6 - suggests that <b><i>ischemi=
a</i></b> may also be present.</li>
</ul>
<div style=3D"text-align: justify;">
<b>CLINICAL IMPRESSION: </b>We would interpret this ECG as showing sinus rh=
ythm with RAD, LAA, RAA, <i>probable </i>RVH, <u>and</u> LVH with "strain" =
<u><i><b>and/or</b></i></u> ischemia <b>(</b><i>which is our way of acknowl=
edging that strain and ischemia may coexist, and ST-T wave changes of one o=
f these may mask the other . . . </i><b>)</b>.&nbsp; <u>Clinically</u> - We=
 strongly suspect a <b><i>dilated </i>cardiomyopathy</b> given the <i>multi=
-</i>chamber enlargement.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: justify;">
-------------------------------</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: justify;">
<span style=3D"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><u><b><span clas=
s=3D"Apple-style-span" style=3D"color: #e06666;">Note</span></b></u> - Many=
 use the terms LAA and LAE/RAA and RAE interchangeably.&nbsp; We prefer <b>=
LAA</b> and <b>RAA (</b><i>left and right atrial <u>A</u>bnormality</i><b>)=
</b> in recognition of the fact that an abnormal-looking P wave will <i>not=
</i> always mean true atrial chamber "<u>E</u>nlargement".</span><br>
-------------------------------<span style=3D"font-size: x-small;">&nbsp;</=
span><br>
<ul>
<li><span style=3D"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">For more inf=
ormation on <b>LVH</b>&nbsp;- Check out <b><a href=3D"http://ecg-interpreta=
tion.blogspot.com/2013/08/ecg-interpretation-review-73-lvh.html" target=3D"=
_blank">ECG Blog #73</a></b>&nbsp;-&nbsp;</span></li>
</ul>
</div>
